>> Currently I play a monk on NAO. When my character became experience
>> level 10 the information about name/rank title disappeared from the
>> status area. A while ago I played a healer with, as I recall
>> correctly, the same behaviour (not exactly sure if also on experience
>> level 10). Is this a NAO related problem or a bug in NetHack? I think
>> the problem corrected itself (when I played the healer) when a new
>> rank title was introduced. I haven't seen it when player other
>> characters (yet). Do you experience the same behaviour?
> 
> I think I've seen players with missing name/rank fields, so I assumed
> it's a configuration setting. If your rank vanishes my guess would be
> that it might be depending on the length of the respective rank text;
> too long rank titles may be suppressed to see the more of the relevant
> parts of the stat line. A look into your and other's config files may
> reveal that mystery.

It's not a configuration option, nor a bug. When the first status line
gets too long, NetHack will remove everything from the beginning of the
line up to (but not including) the "St:"  This is, of course, a tty-only
vanilla feature.

